# Mirrors .gitignore (when .vercelignore exists Vercel ignores .gitignore) +
# the local-only scraper folder, which must never upload to Vercel.
node_modules
dist
.DS_Store
.vercel
.git-hidden
tests/e2e/.auth
playwright-report
test-results
.claude
scraper
# VSL video factory — renders on the VPS, never ships to Vercel (71MB actor
# file broke the 10MB upload limit 2026-07-26). Anchored: a bare `video`
# would also swallow src/features/reviews/video and break the build.
/video
/out
/public/clips
bridge
# HeyPubli is a separate business on its own Vercel project (heypubli-app).
# It only ever lived in this repo for convenience. Elsie must not ship it.
/heypubli
# Local scrape dumps, 12GB of them on 24 Aug 2026. Untracked, so .gitignore
# never saw them, and a prod deploy quietly started uploading SIX GIGABYTES
# before anyone noticed. Anchored, because it is a repo-root folder and a bare
# `exports` would also match anything named exports inside src.
/exports
# Symlink into the local scraper folder (the one-copy strategy doc). The
# target does not exist inside the upload, and Vercel refuses the build on a
# dangling symlink.
/docs/BRRR_STRATEGY.md
